{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"selenium-pugnacious-arcticduck","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nSource comments carry commit SHAs, run/thread IDs, and dated incident narratives that rot: 8 of 18 cited SHAs in the tree are ALREADY unresolvable (Gerrit rebase-on-submit guarantees pre-land SHA death), and run IDs die with retention windows. Policy: source is for current state + concise rationale; the ticket system owns historical detail. Proven detector (0 FPs on current tree): 15 violating sites, 47 compliant blocks.\n\n## Approach\n(1) Remediate the 15 sites — each maps to a specific replacement already adjudicated: delete.py:188 drop dead-SHA mechanism sentence; classify.py:310 + test_frozen_census.py:79 cite epic 3006-e198; reconcile.py:588 + test_commit_binding_store_failure.py describe the failure class (story findable via git log -S); test_ci_actionlint_install.py cite bug 4e99-b2ae; test_plan_review_explain.py cite bug c7e3-dd16; test_execution_mode_dispatch.py cite 454a-9266; test_inbound_differ_field_contract.py point at the live CONTRACT block + story a130-2b7c; 5 PR-#375 sites keep 'PR #375 review' and drop raw thread ids; test_at_most_one_invariant.py:197 drop e04e0b289c. (2) CI guard from the proven detector: block-level scan (comment blocks + AST docstrings); rot-prone = SHA-like hex >=7 with digits+letters (denylist ed25519/sha256 etc), run/job/thread id >=8 digits after keyword, date+evidence-verb; ACCEPTED when the block cites a ticket/epic/story/bug/rec/ADR id (hex-grouped or word-triple alias) — pointing history at the ticket system is the sanctioned pattern; escape hatch 'context: external' for vendor-pinned refs (changelogs, upstream issue SHAs).\n\n## Scope\n- the 15 sites listed above (src/ + tests/)\n- scripts/ or CI lint module implementing the detector + workflow wiring\n- short policy note in CONTRIBUTING.md or docs (source=current state, tickets=history)\n\n## Testing\nDetector unit tests from the proven prototype: the 15 pre-fix sites RED, the 47 compliant blocks green, the acceptor-arm gotchas ('bug surfaced', 'ticket dirs' must NOT accept; grouped 4x4 ids and word-triple aliases MUST accept), escape hatch honored. Post-remediation tree scans clean.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All 15 sites remediated per the mapped replacements; no information lost that isn't reachable via the cited ticket.\n- [ ] CI guard fails on reintroduced rot-prone refs, passes the current remediated tree with zero suppressions.\n- [ ] Escape hatch documented; policy note landed.\n- [ ] Detector unit tests cover the FP gotchas proven in the prototype.","id":"b047-267f-3c3d-4374","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","priority":2,"tags":["hygiene","ci"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Comment hygiene: remediate rot-prone historical refs in code + CI guard"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785640248467756001,"uuid":"d96973bc-b466-4ae7-b4a1-f8f02227cefb"}